# {{projectName}}

Lean workspace based on Amatok, using `@db21/toolkit` conventions.
Requires Node.js 22.16+ and Corepack/Yarn 4.16.0.

## Setup

```sh
corepack yarn install
corepack yarn format
```

Commit the generated `yarn.lock` before enabling CI. CI uses immutable installs.
Bootstrap does not install dependencies, initialize Git, or publish anything.
Templates ship with the toolkit package; generation does not download Amatok.

## Apps

{{#each apps}}
- `apps/{{directory}}`: run `yarn dev:{{directory}}`.
{{/each}}

{{#if hasApi}}
API health endpoint: `/health` on port 3000 (override with `PORT`).
{{/if}}
{{#if hasStatic}}
Astro static site uses port 4321.
{{/if}}
{{#if hasSsr}}
Astro SSR site uses port 4322.
{{/if}}
{{#if hasExpo}}
For Expo native development, run `yarn workspace @{{projectName}}/app ios`
or `yarn workspace @{{projectName}}/app android` with the appropriate simulator/device.
Native builds require the platform-specific Expo toolchain; CI builds Expo web only.
{{/if}}

## Validation

```sh
yarn format:check
yarn lint
yarn check
yarn architecture:check
yarn test
yarn build
```

Only selected apps and their required integrations are included. Database, auth,
GraphQL, business integrations and deployment are intentionally absent. Add tests
alongside new functionality; the initial workspace deliberately has no tests.
The test command accepts an empty suite until meaningful tests are added.
Keep local secrets in ignored environment overrides, never in source files.
